Subject: [PATCH] Preserve resource chooser lifecycle connections during destruction

QObject automatically disconnects signals during its destruction. An early
blanket disconnect unnecessarily removes destroyed observers and triggers
Qt's wildcard-disconnect diagnostic when resource choosers are deleted.

The upstream file retains its original copyright and license notices.

Related upstream issue: https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=509947
The report lists resource chooser wildcard-disconnect diagnostics and the
resulting log-docker reentrancy. This changes chooser destruction, not the
upstream log-handler fix.

diff --git a/libs/resourcewidgets/KisResourceItemChooser.cpp b/libs/resourcewidgets/KisResourceItemChooser.cpp
--- a/libs/resourcewidgets/KisResourceItemChooser.cpp
+++ b/libs/resourcewidgets/KisResourceItemChooser.cpp
@@ -296,7 +296,6 @@
 KisResourceItemChooser::~KisResourceItemChooser()
 {
-    disconnect();
     delete d;
 }
 
 void KisResourceItemChooser::setResponsiveness(bool isResponsive)
